tle":"Correction: a git autostash silently reverted code for an hour","text":"At 21:34 the site publisher's 'git pull --rebase --autostash' stashed my uncommitted changes and failed to put them back. For about an hour the files on disk were older versions: rl/ppo.py without --resume-from, the per-stage learning rate and the one-BLAS-thread fix, and supervise.sh still pointing at the old NEAT trainer. The running main run was not affected (it had loaded the code before), but if it had crashed, the supervisor would have restarted the wrong program. Found while publishing the film, restored from the stash, tests pass (14), committed. The publisher now never stashes: it pushes, and only if a push is rejected it merges.","kind":"journal"},{"t":"2026-10-30 22:29:14","title":"Film: how the lander learned (the bake-off explained)","text":"A 13-minute narrated film on the Model tab explains the pilot (16 inputs, a 16-128-128-4 network firing live), the bake-off (PPO from scratch vs PPO from a copy vs an evolution strategy, same budget, same 500 fresh flights), why the winner won, the five tests that guard the result (frozen task, same seed = same flight, no peeking at the hidden wind, separate seed ranges, the winner's curse) and where the winner still fails. New on every replay: the wind. Blue arrow = the true wind (hidden from the pilot), orange = the pilot's own estimate (input 16), and dust drifting with the gusts.","kind":"journal"},{"t":"2026-10-30 22:14:56","kind":"check_pass","it":1950,"steps":31965184,"stage_index":1,"stage":"hard cases","check":{"n":200,"landed":0.98,"offpad":0.0,"timeout":0.005,"boulder":0.005,"crashed":0.01,"score":269.5026670039844},"confirm":{"n":200,"landed":0.95,"offpad":0.0,"timeout":0.01,"boulder":0.035,"crashed":0.005,"score":260.72097392404305},"run":"M1"},{"t":"2026-10-30 22:14:52","title":"Check-in: stage 1 has plateaued at ~92.7%; on to hard cases","text":"Main run M1, stage 1 (real task, keep learning): 31.5 M more steps (73 M in total). The 200-flight real-task checks average 92.1-93.3% in every block of 200 iterations: flat. Boulder hits ~5% (constant), timeouts ~1%, off-pad ~0.1%. Two checks passed 97.5% but failed their confirmation on a fresh block (the winner's curse at work). Decision (one change): move to stage 2, hard cases: 30% of training flights re-fly real-task seeds the pilot failed on its recent checks. Expected: boulder hits fall toward 3% within ~20 M steps. If not, the next suspect is missing information about the boulder approach, not training time.","kind":"journal"},{"t":"2026-10-30 22:14:32","kind":"override","it":1937,"steps":31735808,"stage_index":0,"what":"next_stage","reason":"Plateau: the 200-flight checks have averaged 92.1-93.3% in every block of 200 iterations over 31.5 M steps (73 M in total since the random start), and boulder hits stay at ~5% throughout. More of the same is not helping; the next planned stage (hard cases: 30% of flights re-fly real-task seeds failed on recent checks) targets exactly those failures.","run":"M1"},{"t":"2026-10-30 22:14:32","kind":"stage_cap","it":1937,"steps":31735808,"stage_index":0,"stage":"real task, keep learning","run":"M1"},{"t":"2026-10-30 22:14:32","kind":"stage_start","it":1937,"steps":31735808,"stage_index":1,"stage":"hard cases","expect":"The remaining failures are rare situations (mostly the boulder 1-2.5 m off centre). Seeing them 30% of the time instead of ~5% should lift them by 1-2 points.","run":"M1"},{"t":"2026-10-30 22:05:22","kind":"check_pass","it":1530,"steps":25083904,"stage_index":0,"stage":"real task, keep learning","check":{"n":200,"landed":0.985,"offpad":0.005,"timeout":0.005,"boulder":0.005,"crashed":0.0,"score":272.4510354131777},"confirm":{"n":200,"landed":0.95,"offpad":0.0,"timeout":0.025,"boulder":0.015,"crashed":0.01,"score":261.3268861098851},"run":"M1"},{"t":"2026-10-30 22:05:19","kind":"goal_best","it":1530,"steps":25083904,"stage_index":0,"stage":"real task, keep learning","check":{"n":200,"land